  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Food is an artifact type. Even though it appears on some creatures, it's never a creature type.",
      "oracle_id": "11f1d2b7-0c2b-40df-bf90-3c55b23449af",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Whatever you do, don't eat the delicious cards.",
      "oracle_id": "11f1d2b7-0c2b-40df-bf90-3c55b23449af",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't sacrifice a Food to pay multiple costs. For example, you can't sacrifice a Food token to activate its own ability and also to activate Maraleaf Rider's ability.",
      "oracle_id": "11f1d2b7-0c2b-40df-bf90-3c55b23449af",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If The Meathook Massacre enters the battlefield and it wasn't cast (or it was cast without paying its mana cost), X will be 0. The first ability will trigger, but it won't be much of a massacre.",
      "oracle_id": "127de52b-df75-4342-95a0-20d84c5bf916",
      "published_at": "2021-09-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Arboreal Alliance's last ability triggers whenever you attack with at least one Elf. You populate exactly once as it resolves, no matter how many Elves you attacked with.",
      "oracle_id": "2f497352-c812-48c4-a922-cc311bcdcdc6",
      "published_at": "2023-11-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Arboreal Alliance enters the battlefield without being cast, or if you cast it with X equal to 0, you'll create a 0/0 green Treefolk creature token. Unless something else is raising its toughness, it will immediately die.",
      "oracle_id": "2f497352-c812-48c4-a922-cc311bcdcdc6",
      "published_at": "2023-11-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any enters-the-battlefield abilities of the copied token will trigger when the new token enters the battlefield. Any \"as [this creature] enters the battlefield\" or \"[this creature] enters the battlefield with\" abilities of the copied token will also work.",
      "oracle_id": "2f497352-c812-48c4-a922-cc311bcdcdc6",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you choose to copy a creature token that's a copy of another creature, the new creature token will copy the characteristics of whatever the original token is copying.",
      "oracle_id": "2f497352-c812-48c4-a922-cc311bcdcdc6",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you control no creature tokens when you populate, nothing will happen.",
      "oracle_id": "2f497352-c812-48c4-a922-cc311bcdcdc6",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Populate doesn't target the creature token you're copying. You choose that creature token as you're taking the populate action. You can choose any creature token you control. If a spell or ability causes you to create a creature token and then instructs you to populate, you may choose to copy the token you just created, or you may choose to copy another creature token you control.",
      "oracle_id": "2f497352-c812-48c4-a922-cc311bcdcdc6",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The new creature token copies the characteristics of the original token as stated by the effect that created the original token.",
      "oracle_id": "2f497352-c812-48c4-a922-cc311bcdcdc6",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The new token doesn't copy whether the original token is tapped or untapped, whether it has any counters on it or Auras and Equipment attached to it, or any noncopy effects that have changed its power, toughness, color, and so on.",
      "oracle_id": "2f497352-c812-48c4-a922-cc311bcdcdc6",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each additional Hardened Scales you control will increase the number of +1/+1 counters placed on a creature you control by one.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a creature you control would enter the battlefield with a number of +1/+1 counters on it, it enters with that many plus one instead.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If two or more effects attempt to modify how many counters would be put on a creature you control, you choose the order to apply those effects, no matter who controls the sources of those effects.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As a copy of a permanent spell resolves, it's put onto the battlefield as a token rather than putting a copy of the spell onto the battlefield. The rules that apply to a permanent spell becoming a permanent apply to a copy of a spell becoming a token.",
      "oracle_id": "c3fdfb94-2d10-4743-864c-a59fdd57d8b7",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a spell has the kindred card type and the chosen creature type, Reflections of Littjara will copy it.",
      "oracle_id": "c3fdfb94-2d10-4743-864c-a59fdd57d8b7",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The token that a resolving copy of a permanent spell becomes isn't \"created.\" Abilities that refer to a copy being created won't interact with the copy resolving.",
      "oracle_id": "c3fdfb94-2d10-4743-864c-a59fdd57d8b7",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The triggered ability and the copy it creates will resolve before the spell that caused the ability to trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "c3fdfb94-2d10-4743-864c-a59fdd57d8b7",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must choose an existing creature type, such as Zombie or Angel. You can't choose card types (e.g., artifact) or supertypes (e.g., snow).",
      "oracle_id": "c3fdfb94-2d10-4743-864c-a59fdd57d8b7",
      "published_at": "2021-02-05",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Gadwick's second ability resolves before the spell that caused it to trigger. It resolves even if that spell is countered.",
      "oracle_id": "c7530ecd-e22f-41e7-a76b-de32809901c8",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Gadwick's triggered ability won't trigger when you cast it because it's not on the battlefield yet.",
      "oracle_id": "c7530ecd-e22f-41e7-a76b-de32809901c8",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Gadwick enters the battlefield without being cast, or if it was cast for a cost other than its mana cost, the value of X for its first ability is 0.",
      "oracle_id": "c7530ecd-e22f-41e7-a76b-de32809901c8",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A creature with ravenous gets its counters as it enters the battlefield. It doesn't enter the battlefield first and then get its counters. Any triggered ability that looks for a creature with a certain power or toughness entering the battlefield will see the counters when it checks to see if it should trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "cdf34da6-d952-43ca-855d-fcd9d49efae6",
      "published_at": "2022-10-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a permanent spell with ravenous is copied, the copy will have the same value for X, and the token permanent that the spell becomes as it enters the battlefield will enter with X counters.",
      "oracle_id": "cdf34da6-d952-43ca-855d-fcd9d49efae6",
      "published_at": "2022-10-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If another permanent enters the battlefield as a copy of a creature with Ravenous, it will not enter with any counters from the ravenous ability.",
      "oracle_id": "cdf34da6-d952-43ca-855d-fcd9d49efae6",
      "published_at": "2022-10-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The triggered ability that checks to see if X is 5 or greater refers to the value of X that was chosen as the spell was cast, which may be different from the number of counters it entered with if there are replacement effects involved. This is also true for any other ability that it has which refers to X and triggers when it enters the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "cdf34da6-d952-43ca-855d-fcd9d49efae6",
